<title>USA: DVI stale raised by Baron group to 21.8pct.</title>
<headline>DVI stale raised by Baron group to 21.8pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group controlled by New York investor Ronald Baron said Monday it has increased its stake in DVI Inc to 21.8 percent or 2,289,250 shares from a last reported 20.8 percent or 2,181,850 shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it acquired the additional shares of the Doylestown, Pa- financial services company between May 8 and June 13 at $11.94 to $14.07 each.</p>
</text>
